WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.069 --> 00:00:06.260
With Hitman Agent 47 out now, let's take a
look at 5 things you probably didn't know

00:00:06.260 --> 00:00:11.889
about the movie based on the hit video game
series.

00:00:11.889 --> 00:00:17.370
Stunt and Fight Co-ordinators Jonathan Eusebio
and Jon Valera created contrasting fight styles

00:00:17.370 --> 00:00:22.820
for Agent 47, who's played by Rupert Friend,
and John Smith, who's played by Zachary Quinto.

00:00:22.820 --> 00:00:27.720
They based John Smith's technique on traditional
Japanese karate and some kickboxing, and gave

00:00:27.720 --> 00:00:29.990
him a haymaker-punching style.

00:00:29.990 --> 00:00:35.500
And to give 47 his own distinct style, they
trained Friend in Malaysian Silat and Filipino

00:00:35.500 --> 00:00:36.760
martial arts.

00:00:36.760 --> 00:00:41.750
As part of his 6 months of training, Friend
also learned boxing, some Judo and Kung-fu,

00:00:41.750 --> 00:00:47.989
and Krav maga which is a form of self-defence
system developed by the Israeli military.

00:00:47.989 --> 00:00:52.540
Friend also did intensive training with the
movie's armaments team to make sure he was

00:00:52.540 --> 00:00:56.910
comfortable with Agent 47's signature weapon,
the Silverballers pistols.

00:00:56.910 --> 00:01:01.230
He even took them home with him to practise,
and, according to the actor, by the end of

00:01:01.230 --> 00:01:05.449
his training, he could take the gun apart
and put it back together again with his eyes

00:01:05.449 --> 00:01:06.449
closed.

00:01:06.449 --> 00:01:10.390
However, Friend still managed to injure himself
on set when he fired his gun into the ground

00:01:10.390 --> 00:01:14.140
by accident and a blank cartridge bounced
up and hit him in the head!

00:01:14.140 --> 00:01:19.400
Despite being hurt, Friend kept filming and
the take actually made it into the final movie!

00:01:19.400 --> 00:01:23.420
But that's not the first time the actor's
got caught out by a gun on set.

00:01:23.420 --> 00:01:28.259
When he was filming Homeland, a stray bullet
from someone else's gun accidentally hit Friend

00:01:28.259 --> 00:01:30.740
in the neck!

00:01:30.740 --> 00:01:35.920
Speaking of Homeland, while filming Hitman
Agent 47, Hannah Ware, who plays Katia van

00:01:35.920 --> 00:01:40.400
Dees in the movie, was pretty persistent in
trying to prise spoilers about Homeland out

00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:45.020
of Rupert Friend, who plays CIA Agent Peter
Quinn on the hit TV show.

00:01:45.020 --> 00:01:50.090
But Friend managed to keep quiet about the
show's future twists and instead had fun teasing

00:01:50.090 --> 00:01:53.270
his curious co-star during the shoot!

00:01:53.270 --> 00:01:58.219
Rupert Friend made a deliberate decision not
to watch the first movie adapted from the

00:01:58.219 --> 00:02:01.530
Hitman video games which was released in 2007.

00:02:01.530 --> 00:02:06.060
Friend avoided the movie which starred Timothy
Olyphant as he didn't want to be influenced

00:02:06.060 --> 00:02:09.790
by someone else's interpretation of his character,
Agent 47.

00:02:09.790 --> 00:02:14.600
Instead, he relied on the video games, and
was particularly influenced by what he describes

00:02:14.600 --> 00:02:20.320
as the "deadly graceful" way Agent 47 moves
in the 2012 instalment, Absolution.

00:02:20.320 --> 00:02:24.520
After experiencing the games, Friend also
felt strongly that the movie should put more

00:02:24.520 --> 00:02:29.190
emphasis on the elements of stealth, cunning
and disguise, and worked with the stunt team

00:02:29.190 --> 00:02:34.020
to include 47's trademark garrotte, or fibre
wire.

00:02:34.020 --> 00:02:39.340
To get Agent 47's signature look right, the
movie's costume designer visited many design

00:02:39.340 --> 00:02:43.200
houses in New York, and also in Germany, where
part of the film was shot.

00:02:43.200 --> 00:02:48.320
But in the end, to get the classic, well-cut
outfit she wanted, she hired a tailor from

00:02:48.320 --> 00:02:52.569
Madrid who flew out to the film's set to create
the suit from scratch.

00:02:52.569 --> 00:02:58.400
Ten black suits, 10 white shirts, and 10 red
ties were custom-made from finely woven cotton

00:02:58.400 --> 00:02:59.650
for the shoot.

00:02:59.650 --> 00:03:03.810
Rupert Friend said that when he put them on,
he "felt like an assassin who's paid millions

00:03:03.810 --> 00:03:04.810
to do his job."

00:03:04.810 --> 00:03:08.620
Now, let me know in the comments below, what
other video games would you like to see on

00:03:08.620 --> 00:03:09.900
the big screen?

00:03:09.900 --> 00:03:13.090
